{
  "page": 5,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Published in Transactions on Machine Learning Research (05/2025)",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        27.39893913269043,
        368.4171447753906,
        37.36153793334961
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        83.52706909179688,
        78.57536315917969,
        94.14328002929688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Method",
      "bbox": [
        91.72608184814453,
        83.52706909179688,
        134.71697998046875,
        94.14328002929688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We will now describe our new D-MPC method. Our approach can be seen as a multi-step diffusion extension",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        111.45991516113281,
        540.211181640625,
        121.42251586914062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of the model-based offline planning (MBOP) paper (Argenson & Dulac-Arnold, 2021), with a few other",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        123.41493225097656,
        540.3701782226562,
        133.37753295898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "modifications and simplifications.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        135.3709259033203,
        217.523681640625,
        145.33352661132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3.1",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        167.4779815673828,
        86.00741577148438,
        176.32476806640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Model predictive control",
      "bbox": [
        96.96627807617188,
        167.4779815673828,
        208.46771240234375,
        176.32476806640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "D-MPC first learns the dynamics model ps|a, action proposal π and heuristic value function J (see below), in",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        189.94593811035156,
        540.0379638671875,
        201.0679473876953
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "an offline phase, as we discuss in Section 3.2, and then proceeds to alternate between taking an action in the",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        201.90089416503906,
        540.2304077148438,
        211.86349487304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "environment with planning the next sequence of actions using a planner, as we discuss in Section 3.3. The",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        213.8559112548828,
        540.2459106445312,
        223.81851196289062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "overall MPC pseudocode is provided in Algorithm 1.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        225.81092834472656,
        301.8570861816406,
        235.77352905273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3.2",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        257.9189758300781,
        86.00741577148438,
        266.7657470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Model learning",
      "bbox": [
        96.96627807617188,
        257.9189758300781,
        164.8614044189453,
        266.7657470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We assume access to an offline dataset of trajectories, consisting of (state, action, reward) triples: D =",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        280.38690185546875,
        540.001953125,
        290.3495178222656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "{s1",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        291.8920593261719,
        86.24209594726562,
        302.2447509765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:T1, a1",
      "bbox": [
        82.27400207519531,
        291.89208984375,
        112.29409790039062,
        305.0184020996094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:T1, r2",
      "bbox": [
        108.32600402832031,
        291.8921203613281,
        136.81210327148438,
        305.0184326171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:T1, s2",
      "bbox": [
        132.5670166015625,
        291.89215087890625,
        161.57411193847656,
        305.0184631347656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:T2, a2",
      "bbox": [
        157.60601806640625,
        291.8921813964844,
        187.6260986328125,
        305.01849365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:T2, rm",
      "bbox": [
        183.6580047607422,
        291.85736083984375,
        215.2474365234375,
        305.0185241699219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:T2, . . . sM",
      "bbox": [
        207.89901733398438,
        291.8573913574219,
        253.8164825439453,
        305.0185546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:TM , aM",
      "bbox": [
        246.22201538085938,
        291.857421875,
        283.4175109863281,
        305.990966796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:TM , rM",
      "bbox": [
        275.8230285644531,
        291.8574523925781,
        311.4845275878906,
        305.9909973144531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1:TM }. We then use this to fit a diffusion-based dynamics",
      "bbox": [
        303.613037109375,
        292.3419189453125,
        540.10791015625,
        305.99102783203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model pd(st+1:t+F |st, ht, at:t+F −1) and another diffusion-based action proposal ρ(at:t+F −1|st, ht). To fit",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        304.2969055175781,
        540.2732543945312,
        315.6947326660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "these models, we minimize the denoising score matching loss in the usual way. We include a detailed review",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        316.25189208984375,
        540.592041015625,
        326.2145080566406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of diffusion model training in Appendix A, and refer the readers to e.g. Karras et al. (2022) for additional",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        328.2079162597656,
        540.2052612304688,
        338.1705322265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "discussions.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        340.16290283203125,
        122.08198547363281,
        350.1255187988281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We also define a function J that approximates the reward-to-go given any proposed sequence of states and",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        358.0959167480469,
        540.16064453125,
        368.05853271484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "actions:",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        370.0509033203125,
        105.28504180908203,
        380.0135192871094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "J(st:t+F , at:t+F −1) = E[",
      "bbox": [
        177.56300354003906,
        396.784912109375,
        282.7405700683594,
        408.1817321777344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "t+F −1",
      "bbox": [
        282.7879638671875,
        387.0706481933594,
        308.2330322265625,
        393.6539001464844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "X",
      "bbox": [
        288.31695556640625,
        394.8915100097656,
        302.7129211425781,
        401.267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "k=t",
      "bbox": [
        288.7469482421875,
        411.898193359375,
        302.2796325683594,
        418.0909118652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "γk−tR(sk, ak) + γF V (st+F )]",
      "bbox": [
        309.8969421386719,
        393.7269592285156,
        434.4399719238281,
        408.24151611328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(2)",
      "bbox": [
        528.4349365234375,
        396.784912109375,
        541.1671142578125,
        406.7475280761719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Here γ is the discount factor, and V (s) represents the value function from state s (i.e., estimate of future",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        431.73291015625,
        540.055908203125,
        441.6955261230469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reward at the leaves of this search process). We also use a transformer to learn J (although we can also just",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        443.6878967285156,
        540.3143920898438,
        453.6505126953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "compute J directly, if the reward function R is known, and we use an admissible lower bound (such as 0) on",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        455.6429138183594,
        540.1265869140625,
        465.60552978515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "V ) by regressing from (st:t+F , at:t+F −1) to the discounted future reward in Eq. (2). We use L2 loss for the",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        467.597900390625,
        540.146728515625,
        478.9947204589844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "regression. We use J as the objective function for optimization in MPC, and as a way to specify novel tasks.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        479.55291748046875,
        542.1068725585938,
        489.5155334472656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Refer to Appendix E for additional details on model architectures and hyperparameters.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        491.5079040527344,
        458.0507507324219,
        501.47052001953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Algorithm 1: Main MPC loop.",
      "bbox": [
        71.56500244140625,
        523.158935546875,
        212.67910766601562,
        533.1215209960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1 Input: D = offline dataset, N = num. samples, F = forecast horizon, H = history length",
      "bbox": [
        62.505001068115234,
        538.2459106445312,
        460.0000305175781,
        548.20849609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2 (pd, ρ, J) = train(D)",
      "bbox": [
        62.504974365234375,
        550.201904296875,
        159.95144653320312,
        561.0189208984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3 s0 = env.init()",
      "bbox": [
        62.50498962402344,
        562.1569213867188,
        135.4732208251953,
        573.6134643554688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4 h0 = (s0)",
      "bbox": [
        62.50498962402344,
        574.1119384765625,
        113.91544342041016,
        585.5684814453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "5 for t = 0 : ∞do",
      "bbox": [
        62.5049934387207,
        586.06689453125,
        144.81158447265625,
        596.0294799804688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "6",
      "bbox": [
        62.90399932861328,
        601.0894165039062,
        67.41604614257812,
        607.3449096679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "at = planner.plan(st, ht, pd, ρ, J, N, F, H)",
      "bbox": [
        87.34199523925781,
        598.0219116210938,
        266.90643310546875,
        609.4794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "7",
      "bbox": [
        62.90397644042969,
        613.04443359375,
        67.41602325439453,
        619.2999267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(st+1, rt+1) = env.step(st, at)",
      "bbox": [
        87.34197998046875,
        609.9769287109375,
        216.04942321777344,
        620.794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "8",
      "bbox": [
        62.903961181640625,
        625.0004272460938,
        67.41600799560547,
        631.2559204101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ht = append(at, st+1, rt+1)",
      "bbox": [
        87.34295654296875,
        621.9329223632812,
        206.00540161132812,
        633.3894653320312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "9",
      "bbox": [
        62.90394592285156,
        636.9554443359375,
        67.4159927368164,
        643.2109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ht = suffix(ht, H)",
      "bbox": [
        87.34294128417969,
        633.887939453125,
        165.2364044189453,
        645.344482421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Note that unlike MBOP (Argenson & Dulac-Arnold, 2021) we do not need to train ensembles, since diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        674.0709228515625,
        540.1919555664062,
        684.0335083007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "models are expressive enough to capture the richness of the respective distributions directly. Also, in contrast",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        686.02587890625,
        540.5530395507812,
        695.9884643554688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to Argenson & Dulac-Arnold (2021), we do not need to train a separate reward function: we estimate our",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        697.9808959960938,
        540.3756103515625,
        707.9434814453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "value function at the beginning of the planning horizon, for a given sequence of states and actions along that",
      "bbox": [
        71.74099731445312,
        709.9368896484375,
        540.5065307617188,
        719.8994750976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "horizon. In this way, our objective function J already includes the estimated reward along the horizon.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        721.8919067382812,
        521.7218017578125,
        731.8544921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "5",
      "bbox": [
        303.50897216796875,
        751.7799072265625,
        308.4902648925781,
        761.7424926757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
  ],
